course: dictionary
lesson: 8677
title: Sedimentary: rock made in layers
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sedimentary is a word you will meet when you study rocks. Look at the words around it: «In undisturbed sedimentary rock, the lowest layers are the oldest.» Layers are the clue. Sedimentary rock is built in layers, like a stack of pancakes.
explain: Rocks belong to three families: igneous, sedimentary and metamorphic. Igneous rock comes from melted rock, and metamorphic rock is changed by heat and pressure. So sedimentary rock must be the third kind, made in a different way.
explain: The word sediment is the key. Sediment is the bits that settle at the bottom of water, such as sand, mud and shells. «Most fossils are found in sedimentary rocks, because living things were buried in the layers.» Sedimentary means made from sediment.
fact: Sedimentary rock is made from layers of sand, mud, shells or tiny bits of other rock.
fact: These layers are pressed together over a very long time until they turn into solid rock.
fact: Sandstone, limestone, chalk and shale are all sedimentary rocks.
fact: Most fossils form when a dead plant or animal is buried quickly in mud or sand, so fossils are mostly found in sedimentary rock.
fact: In undisturbed sedimentary rock, the lowest layers are the oldest.
exercise: What is sedimentary rock made from? | *Layers of sand, mud, shells or tiny bits of rock | Gas bubbles from a volcano | Melted rock that has cooled | Heat and pressure that changed it
exercise: Sedimentary means made from sediment. What is sediment? | Hot liquid rock from a volcano | *Bits that settle at the bottom of water | A very old tree | Bits of metal inside a machine
exercise: «Most fossils are found in sedimentary rocks.» Why is that? | It is the hardest rock on Earth | Fossils are made of melted rock | *Living things were buried in its layers | It is the newest kind of rock
test: Which of these is a sedimentary rock? | Marble | Granite | *Chalk | Basalt
test: «In undisturbed sedimentary rock, the lowest layers are the oldest.» Which layers are the oldest? | The layers at the edge | *The lowest layers | The middle layers | The top layers
exam: Which statement is true? | Fossils are never found in rock | *All rocks belong to three families, and sedimentary is one of them | Sedimentary rock is made only by volcanoes | Sedimentary rock is made of melted rock
